cases
requirement	case	module	access program	error	reason	output	diagnostic	assertion
void-os.1	1	void-os	void-os			false	false	a hook's input is kept as relations in normal form, each record beginning with its primary key
void-os.2	1	void-os	void-os			true	false	what is new is the values stored less those communicated to the session and agent it is asked for
void-os.3	1	void-os	void-os		keeping failed<LF>	false	true	an error that ends an access program a module calls ends the module's access as that error: keeping failed from storage ends the view, and the command
void-os.4	1	void-os	void-os			false	false	a name taken from outside that begins with _ is written with that _ doubled: the input's file
void-os.5	1	void-os	void-os				false	the command takes its operands as its arguments
void-os.6	1	void-os	void-os			true	false	with no operand the command serves MCP over the standard streams until its standard input ends
void-os.7	1	void-os	void-os			false	false	a hook event as the one operand runs that hook, handed the working directory, and ends with exit status 0
void-os.8	1	void-os	void-os		usage: void-os [view [--filter filter] [input [day [position]]] | hook-event]<LF>	false	true	other operands write the usage message, then LF, on standard error and end with exit status 1
void-os.9	1	void-os	void-os				true	a hook that fails ends with exit status 1, never 2
void-os.10	1	void-os	void-os			true	false	view as the first operand runs the view, handed whether standard output is a terminal
void-os.11	1	void-os	void-os		no input /no/such<LF>		true	an error the view raises is written by its reason, then LF, on standard error and ends with exit status 1
